    <string name="app_on_plan_adds_a_step_more_adds_two_less_s_0e809a81">“On plan” adds a step, “more” adds two, “less” steps back the movement that made it hard. An exact number for a single exercise outweighs the overall rating — and when your sets show more than the plan, the next plan starts from what you showed. Nothing is estimated: whatever you are given, you have already done. The plan climbs at most two steps per workout — and only one wherever the tissue doing the work needs the slower pace: tendons remodel on a longer clock than muscle. A step lands on one set, not on all of them.</string>
